multi-horizon projections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations from ingredients, calculating nutrition and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level daily feed plans based on bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Log feeding activity, calculate variances and costs, decrement inventory, and roll up lot consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements as a time series.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate and update feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards and reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report with lot comparisons, filters, and CSV or PDF export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Create sample/mock data and a yard-level summary dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Deliver the proposed solution, architecture, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the feed-to-gain report and its exports follow the same yard and profitability access rules as dashboards?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Restrict report results and exports to the user's authorized yards and apply the same profitability restrictions as dashboards.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to access operational records and role-based permissions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use email and password sign-in for the web app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may import source records and change PO-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with operational access can import source records and change mappings; other users can view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may change target weights and growth-rate assumptions used for forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized managers can change the assumptions; other users can view forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain inventory items, record receipts or adjustments, and change the wastage setting?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized inventory users may make these changes; operational users may view inventory and record feeding subject to stock controls.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with authorized ration-management access may perform these actions; other users may view rations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should feed-plan creation or adjustment permissions differ from updating a plan's execution status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized planners generate or adjust plans; operators may update execution status for their assigned pens.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may add weight measurements to a lot's history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only authorized livestock or operations users may add measurements; other users may view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive feedlot web app with email-and-password sign-in that displays the returned landing page, navigation, and actions according to the signed-in user’s permissions, or shows the authentication error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized operational users preview and import selected mock procurement and receiving records through the documented adapter, showing source fields and the returned import results, counts, and matched records without presenting matches as new duplicates; show imported records but no enabled import action to users without operational access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized operational users map PO lines to lots and lots to pens, retain and display allocated animal quantities and returned pen details, and show saved values or service errors while preserving the last saved mappings when a save fails; show existing mappings without change actions to users without operational access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Display market-date and target-weight forecasts using incoming animal data and yard defaults, applying lot-specific overrides when present; show projected dates as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and limit forecast-assumption editing to authorized managers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Display feed inventory items, stock movements, quantities, costs, nutritional values, storage, wastage settings, and stock values; let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts and adjustments, and change wastage settings, while users with view-only access see values without enabled edit actions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual inventory projections from available stock, saved upcoming feed plans, and configured wastage; display empty states when plans are unavailable and list known actual wastage separately from delivered-feed consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve rations, and display ingredient proportions, nutrition, and calculated cost; identify the lowest-cost candidate meeting selected nutritional requirements, with a separate save action, and do not treat an unsaved candidate as a saved ration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized planners generate or adjust dated pen-level feed plans using selected bunk rates, rations, and animal counts, and display returned plan details and execution status; users without planning access see existing plans without generation or adjustment actions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Flag saved plans for review when relevant inputs change without changing saved values; let authorized planners confirm updates or regenerate plans, let assigned-pen operators update execution status, and show actual intake and variance without automatically rewriting the plan.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot, including per-lot allocations for pens containing multiple lots, and display returned variance, cost, energy, ingredient inventory consumption, status, and cumulative lot consumption and cost; keep known wastage separate from delivered feed and display stock errors without showing refused events as saved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized livestock or operations users add lot weight measurements and display returned, time-ordered measurement history and gain information; users without entry access see the history without an enabled add action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Display returned lot performance metrics for days on feed, weight gain, average daily gain, feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date; show the date as unavailable without positive ADG and refresh metrics from returned values after feeding or weight records change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Present explainable, rule-based feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions based on lot weight-gain trends, without changing plans or sale dates unless an authorized planner explicitly acts; show the returned basis and response status, and leave saved plans unchanged when access is unavailable or a change is refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Display dashboard values for yard and lot performance, inventory, rations, feeding, weights, costs, and energy, including best- and worst-performing lots; let users select FCR, ADG, or cost of gain as the ranking measure and show returned empty-data states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability that show feed use, lot performance, ration use, plan variance, inventory, and cost of gain, and export filtered results as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict dashboards, reports, and exports to records and profitability fields returned for the signed-in user’s authorized yards and permissions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and CSV or PDF exports of filtered results subject to returned permissions; show the sex filter as unavailable for records without sex data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an on-screen, filterable lot profitability list limited to authorized yards, export its filtered results as CSV, and hide profitability values when the service indicates the user cannot view them.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized users load visibly designated sample data without duplicates, display returned operation results, and require confirmation before reset or replacement; users without sample-data management permission see sample records without enabled management actions, and refused operations display the returned error while retaining the existing list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost using returned aggregate values, with explicit unavailable values for missing metrics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a delivery overview or presentation page with sections or links for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every web-app page works responsively at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page overflow; use touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels on narrow screens.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}